# .understandignore — patterns for files/dirs to exclude from analysis
# Syntax: same as .gitignore (globs, # comments, ! negation, trailing / for dirs)
#
# SCOPE: only internal/ core (biz / data / service / server / job / conf), with tests.
# Everything outside internal/ is excluded to keep the knowledge graph focused
# on business code, not boilerplate.

# --- Top-level dirs outside internal/ ---
api/
cmd/
configs/
deploy/
docs/
pkg/
scripts/
test/
third_party/

# --- Root-level files ---
# NOTE: go.mod is intentionally NOT excluded — the import-map resolver needs it
# to resolve module-prefix imports.
go.sum
Makefile
openapi.yaml
docker-compose.yml
*.yml
*.yaml
README.md

# --- Generated / mock code inside internal/ ---
*.pb.go
*.pb.validate.go
wire_gen.go
internal/mocks/
**/mocks/

# --- Go build artifacts & local secrets ---
bin/
*.exe
*.test
*.out
.DS_Store
*.key
*.cert
tmp/
.cursor/
.codegraph/
